      "evidence": "template/scripts/pr_review_gate.py retry_unavailable increments attempts[f\"{kind}-unavailable\"] and sets next_job=None once streak >= MAX_ROUNDS. The only reset in the diff is in reoffer(), which sets set_attempts {f\"{kind}-unavailable\": 0}. A candidate with two unavailable attempts in round 1, a successful repair, then one unavailable attempt in round 2 would reach 3 and lose its automatic retry. The completion-lifecycle spec says 'three consecutive attempts'. I did not see the review-side reset path, so this is unconfirmed.",
      "id": "unavailable-streak-not-reset-on-success",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "The repair-unavailable streak counter is reset only by switch-provider or resume. Nothing in the diff resets it when a later repair round succeeds, so the bound on consecutive unavailable attempts may carry across rounds."
